<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbey of Saint-Martin of Tours</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abbey of Saint-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-tours">Martin of Tours</a> grew up around the tomb of Saint Martin, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, who died in 397, and became one of the greatest pilgrimage churches of Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcuin-of-york">Alcuin</a> was its abbot from 796 to 804, and later the Robertian dukes, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a>, held it as lay abbots. The medieval basilica was demolished after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>, and a new basilica now marks the tomb.</p></div>
